# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: mayo-shake256-return-type
why: fips202.h declares `int shake256(...)` but fips202.c (which does not include it) defines `void shake256(...)`.
why: x86/ARM ignore the mismatch; wasm checks function types, so mayo.c's `drop` of the missing result makes the
why: module invalid ("type mismatch: expected a type but nothing on stack" in mayo_keypair_compact, every MAYO
why: wasm32 binary, CI runs up to 45581879065). No caller uses the result. The patch declares the function as
why: it is defined (void); the definition and every caller compile unchanged.
file: upstream/src/common/fips202.h
count: 1
find: int shake256(unsigned char *output, size_t outputByteLen, const unsigned char *input, size_t inputByteLen);
replace: void shake256(unsigned char *output, size_t outputByteLen, const unsigned char *input, size_t inputByteLen);
